    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0535" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg463"/>

                <head>No. 280.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Reed</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 27,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter from Mr. Henry
                    Beste, of New York, and of the protest dated the 20th instant, made by him
                    against the payment of an impost exacted by the Spanish consul at New York, on
                    the cargo shipped by him on the American schooner Clara Fletcher, L. I Sargent,
                    master, bound for Arroyos, Porto Rico, of ten cents for each and every 1,000
                    kilograms weight of said cargo, amounting to $17.10. The legation will make use
                    of this case, in connection with the other similar ones it has in charge,
                    according to its best judgment.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d344-a2.xml" xpointer="d344-a2"/>
